    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d887">

                <pb facs="0834" n="744" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg744"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1014</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-01-28T20:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 28,
                                1918, 8 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 29, 9.58
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1389. Have just seen Minister for Foreign Affairs who informed me that Finnish
                    government had notified Swedish representative in Helsingfors that it could not
                    longer be responsible for lives of Swedish subjects and Swedish representative
                    has left Helsingfors on special train. Viborg is entirely in the hands of
                    Bolsheviks, Helsingfors soon will be, and St. Petersburg Bolsheviks have
                    promised assistance. He added that Swedish delegate was watching internal
                    situation closely, fearing spread of Bolshevik propaganda in Sweden.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
